WEBVTT

NOTE Visual text from a silent video.

1
00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:07.400
The model can write “draft ready” without saving a document.

2
00:00:07.400 --> 00:00:14.100
The tool must create the draft and return its identifier.

3
00:00:14.100 --> 00:00:22.000
Check the result in the system, not only in the final sentence.

4
00:00:22.700 --> 00:00:29.400
A name search can return two different customers.

5
00:00:29.400 --> 00:00:36.100
The agent observes the ambiguity and changes plan: it asks for an identifier.

6
00:00:36.100 --> 00:00:44.000
The next action depends on what has just happened.

7
00:00:44.700 --> 00:00:51.400
The task permits reading invoices, calculating and preparing a draft.

8
00:00:51.400 --> 00:00:58.100
Sending the message is a different action and needs separate authorization.

9
00:00:58.100 --> 00:01:06.000
The agent cannot expand its own permissions to finish sooner.

10
00:01:06.700 --> 00:01:13.400
Two runs can end with the same invoice total.

11
00:01:13.400 --> 00:01:20.100
One saves a draft; the other sends it without permission.

12
00:01:20.100 --> 00:01:28.000
The same final text does not imply the same evaluation result.

13
00:01:28.700 --> 00:01:35.400
An external source can mix useful data with a malicious instruction.

14
00:01:35.400 --> 00:01:42.100
The instruction tries to influence an available tool.

15
00:01:42.100 --> 00:01:50.000
Runtime policy must limit which actions can execute.

16
00:01:50.700 --> 00:01:57.400
Accepting an operation only confirms that the system received it.

17
00:01:57.400 --> 00:02:04.100
Conversation can continue while the tool is working.

18
00:02:04.100 --> 00:02:12.000
Only a verified result supports reporting that the task finished.
